[
  {
    "sha": "d4b0445f71099ed17b99e5ff09d58ecd6459971f",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGQ0YjA0NDVmNzEwOTllZDE3Yjk5ZTVmZjA5ZDU4ZWNkNjQ1OTk3MWY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T22:17:15Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T22:17:15Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): march sideways rapids along their whole length\n\nLaw (d) judged a lateral rapid under the clearance plane at its start,\nmidpoint and end only, and on 2.5-D paths hidden_along returns early\nwith no model - so a floor-depth link between two pockets whose three\nsamples stood in cut air drove through the uncut wall between them and\nposted.\n\nThe column reading now marches the rapid at stations every d / RINGS\n(the footprint's ring spacing, floored at 0.01 mm), both ends included,\nand applies the #106 footprint test at each, with or without a model.\nThe footprint reaches d ahead of and behind each station, so no wall\nslips between stations (step minus reach is non-positive); the only\nremaining bound is the footprint's own sampling. A rapid needing more\nthan 2^18 stations fails closed (convicted) rather than being thinned.\n\nPinned by sideways_rapids: the issue's 4 mm wall and a 1 mm wall are\nrefused; a 68 mm link over a fully cut slot stays clean.\n\nFixes #140\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
